domain GoalCorrection:
  description "Correct the goal criterion without changing runtime."
problem P1:
  |
    Proposed ADR0028 rev1 confuses goal appropriateness with owner provenance.
evidence E1:
  |
    Owner now explicitly states that author confirmation does not matter;
    a goal must be legitimate in light of character personality and relationship.
evidence E2:
  |
    Requirement v1 R1 makes author-explicit defaultObjective binding; ADR0028
    D1 adds envelopeV3, owner reconfirmation and unknown-origin start rejection.
    ADR status is Proposed. Existing immutable V1/V2 contracts remain unchanged.
premise BOUNDARY:
  |
    Owner requests ADR correction or supersession. Document correction and its
    dependencies are in scope, not runtime, paid execution or publication.
    New requirement bytes cannot inherit old review or acceptance.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, BOUNDARY:
  |
    Correct Proposed ADR0028 as revision 2, not supersede an Accepted ADR.
    Preserve old content via Seal history and a correction record. Create requirement
    v2 candidate plus exact review input at step1, retaining v1 as historical accepted
    bytes but explicitly naming its conflicting R1 as displaced by the current owner
    instruction. Do not claim v2 or ADR acceptance or run independent review.
decision D2 based_on D1, E1:
  |
    Goal derivation evaluates personality, values and known counterpart relationship
    in the existing conscious call, regardless of source or owner confirmation.
    Existing objective text is context, not privileged authority. Victory is ordinary
    fallback where compatible. Keep engine prohibitions and immutable battle binding.
    Remove origin fields, new character envelope, reconfirmation UI and origin-block
    errors. Goal basis/rationale and F01/F02 semantic quality evaluation remain;
    reference validation alone cannot prove semantic legitimacy. No new critic call.
decision D3 based_on D1, D2:
  |
    Inspect Seal impact before changes, update affected design/plan/PERT and tests
    planned for provenance into semantic-fit cases. Preserve historical reviews,
    acceptance and evidence as snapshots. Reseal only inspected active dependencies,
    verify original bytes, stale scan and fsck. Stop at requirement/ADR review gates.
